+# Handoff: FunctionGram — complete work + clickable hashtags/mentions
+
+## What this is
+
+Everything built in this session is captured in **one file**:
+
+- **`FunctionGram-full-work.patch`** — the complete, verified diff
+  (47 files: all 15 sections of the implementation prompt **plus** the
+  clickable `#hashtag` / `@mention` feature). It was generated from commit
+  `7402123` on branch `arena/01a0e625-functiongram`, diffed against the
+  original base commit `c4d3d75` ("Add files via upload").
+
+The patch was proven to apply cleanly on a fresh clone of the base
+(`git apply --check` → no errors, no warnings).
+
+## Why a file?
+
+This session's GitHub connection is closed (the session ended when its PR
+was merged/closed), so it **cannot push**. The local workspace was also
+reset to the base commit — so the work was re-committed locally as
+`7402123` on `arena/01a0e625-functiongram` and exported to the patch file
+above.
+
+## Option 1 — new Arena coding session (easiest, recommended)
+
+Start a new coding session in `rstmcsoch/FunctionGram` and tell the agent:
+
+> "The repo's local branch `arena/01a0e625-functiongram` has one unpushed
+> commit (`7402123`) with the complete FunctionGram work. Fetch from GitHub,
+> rebase it onto the remote branch (so it lands on top of what's already
+> there), then push to `origin/arena/01a0e625-functiongram`. If the remote
+> branch no longer exists, just push it as-is. Then update or reopen the
+> PR (or open a new one) so the work is reviewable."
+
+The commands that will do it (for reference):
+
+```bash
+git fetch origin
+git rebase origin/arena/01a0e625-functiongram   # merges cleanly; the old work is already on the remote
+git push origin arena/01a0e625-functiongram
+```
+
+If the old remote branch was deleted, skip the rebase and push directly.
+
+## Option 2 — apply the patch on your own machine
+
+If PR #8 is **still open** (or was closed without merging):
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/rstmcsoch/FunctionGram && cd FunctionGram
+git checkout <branch or main at commit c4d3d75>
+git apply FunctionGram-full-work.patch
+git add -A && git commit -m "Complete FunctionGram fixes + clickable hashtags/mentions"
+git push   # and open/update the PR
+```
+
+If PR #8 was **merged** (main already contains the earlier work):
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/rstmcsoch/FunctionGram && cd FunctionGram
+git checkout -b fg-followup main
+git apply --3way FunctionGram-full-work.patch   # 3-way merge skips what's already in main
+git add -A && git commit -m "Clickable #hashtags and @mentions"
+git push -u origin fg-followup   # then open a PR for this branch
+```
+
+## What was verified (before packaging)
+
+| Check | Result |
+| --- | --- |
+| Live API smoke — 25 checks (hashtag matching incl. whole-word + case-insensitive, reel-in/story-out, tag validation 400s, guest/public rules, @mention resolution, unknown handles stay plain text, post create/edit/delete round-trip) | 25/25 PASS |
+| `tsc --noEmit` (strict) | 0 errors |
+| `npm run lint` | 0 errors (11 pre-existing warnings) |
+| `npm run test:vercel` | 25/25 |
+| `npm run build` | ✓ all routes |
+| `git apply --check` on fresh base clone | clean |
+
+Details in `VERIFICATION.md`.
+
+## The hashtag/mention feature in one line
+
+`#tags` render dark blue and open `#/tag/<name>` — a page listing every
+post + reel using the tag (`GET /api/social?hashtag=<tag>`); `@mentions`
+render in a red-pink gradient and open the tagged person's profile
+(unknown handles stay plain text). Captions tokenize in feed cards, post
+viewer, stories, and the reels player.
