+  case-insensitive whole-word match on the caption
+  (`(^|[^a-z0-9_])#tag($|[^a-z0-9_])`), and the tag is validated before it is
+  interpolated, so the regex is safe. `discovery:true` (kind != story) keeps
+  posts + reels only, and the standard privacy/blocked guards apply. Like the
+  other public discovery endpoints (`?explore`, `?search`, `?profile`), guests
+  can browse hashtag pages while private accounts stay hidden from them;
+  personal endpoints (e.g. `?following`) still 401 for guests.
+
+Client routing: `#/tag/<name>` (hash route, tag name rides the existing
+profile-id slot). The `tag` view was added to the `View` union and the allowed
+route list.
+
+Verified with a live HTTP smoke test against the running dev server
+(`.smoke-hashtag.mjs`, run as the local `you.preview` account): 25/25 checks —
+seeded + freshly created posts matched by tag, whole-word + case-insensitive
+matching, reel included / story excluded, empty/invalid/overlong → 400, guest
+can browse (public) but `?following` still 401, mention target present in the
+people list (so it links) while an unknown handle is not, and cleanup
+(delete) restores state. All gates green after the change: `tsc` 0 errors,
+lint 0 errors, `npm run test:vercel` 25/25, `npm run build` compiles. CSS
+classes `.hashtag`/`.mention` are new and do not collide with the existing
+`.tag-*` (people-tag-picker) styles.
+
+## Remaining risks
+
+- Live email delivery, real Blob uploads, and Neon connectivity still need a
+  one-time check against production resources after env is wired (build and
+  fail-closed behavior are verified without them).
+- The local preview uses a gitignored `.env.local` with dummy Brevo values and
+  a local `BETTER_AUTH_URL`; production relies on the trusted-origin config
+  described above — custom domains must be added to `AUTH_TRUSTED_ORIGINS`.
